## Research Overview

This MSc thesis investigates the dynamical characteristics of the Southwest Asia Subtropical Jet from the perspective of atmospheric wave activity.

The analysis was performed using Fortran-based calculations and GrADS visualization tools.

## Main Results

### Temperature Profiles
Selected vertical temperature profiles are presented to investigate the thermal structure associated with jet dynamics.

### Jet Structure
The spatial distribution and evolution of the Southwest Asia Jet are analyzed using atmospheric circulation fields.

### Wave Activity
Wave activity diagnostics are used to examine the interaction between planetary waves and jet dynamics.

### Flux Analysis
The fluxes across a defined control volume around the jet are investigated to identify regions of stronger incoming and outgoing energy transport.
